Actually, I rarely bother anymore. I haven't written a genocide scroll in
a long time, and I tend to find only one or two along the way. If I find
a scroll and ID it without reading, I'll bless it and kill ;'s, just
because I find them annoying. Otherwise, given a single monster type to
kill, I'll blow the ML's away just on general principles.

All of the standard candidates for genocide (Vampire Lords, cockatrices,
etc) I find too useful to eradicate. I rarely get level drained or
stoned; I'm just too good :).

All in all, for me the balance is OK because I'd rather use magic markers
to write enchant and charging scrolls. Oh, yeah; spellbooks, too.
Identify and magic mapping are just too convenient.

Sure, you can luck out and end up with six or seven blessed genocides,
but I think that's rare enough to preserve balance.

>Has anyone out there ascended without genociding ANY species?

